Subject: [PATCH 6/7] Show a refused trajectory read as a refusal, and nothing
 else
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A 403 or 404 left the whole canvas mounted under the denial banner: the
ATT&CK strip still reading 'Loading ATT&CK mapping', zero indicators, a
device Actions menu, an events-loaded counter and an empty timeline.
Unavailable evidence therefore looked like a completed investigation of
a quiet endpoint.

A refusal of THIS read now IS the page: what was refused, which device
and window were asked for, the fact that an empty trajectory here says
nothing about the device, and the way back to the XDR incident the
analyst arrived from. NO_CUSTOMER is deliberately not treated this way
— the analyst only has to pick a customer, so the canvas stays.
